suggestion_id|category|suggestion|reasoning|priority|recommended_path|status|official_source_url
A10-S01|Prices|Close the price gap before building anything else|Every other improvement is unmeasurable without opening and closing prices. Ten more strategies evaluated on probability scoring will still not tell us whether we can beat a number.|Highest. This is the binding constraint on the whole programme.|Licence a price feed; until then keep everything in paper and rank on Brier score only.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-10
A10-S02|Results|Recover 2026 week 4 and re-run the reconciliation|16 games are missing from a 136-game season. That is a hole in the training data for every club.|High - it is a small, well-defined task with an exact success test (captured PF/PA must equal published PF/PA).|Retry the week-4 scores page, then fall back to per-club schedule pages.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-4
A10-S03|Depth|Automate weekly capture of all 32 club depth charts|Only 4 of 32 charts were readable as text this session, which is why the depth-fade strategy produced 2 signals and cannot be scored.|High among the original signals - this is the one thing in this pack that no generic odds feed would give us.|A weekly scraper over <club>.com/team/depth-chart with a per-club render check; flag any club whose chart renders as an image.|not_started|https://www.packers.com/team/depth-chart
A10-S04|Origination|Shrink the ratings toward the mean|Split-season margin stability is low, which means a large part of each rating is noise. Unshrunk ratings produce confident bets on lucky teams.|Medium-high. Cheap to do and it should improve out-of-sample log-loss immediately.|Use the observed split-season correlation to set the shrinkage factor; re-estimate weekly and publish the factor.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-1
A10-S05|Staking|Cap the Kelly fraction and separate the staking columns permanently|The martingale row in the leaderboard turned a losing signal into a paper profit right up until a drawdown that would have ended it. That is exactly the failure mode the separation is meant to expose.|High as a governance matter - it costs nothing and prevents the most likely way this programme loses money.|Cap any Kelly-derived stake at a fixed fraction of bankroll, and never let a staking result influence the signal ranking.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-1
A10-S06|Validation|Switch the primary skill metric from win rate to closing-line value|At -110 the break-even is 52.38%, and detecting a 5-point edge takes roughly a thousand settled bets. CLV converges far faster because it does not need results.|High, once prices exist. Until then use log-loss and Brier.|Compute mean CLV over the trailing window and wire it into the demotion gate as rule A4-D02.|blocked_on_prices|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-10
A10-S07|Origination|Model team totals jointly instead of splitting the game total by the margin|The pack currently derives team totals algebraically as (total ± margin)/2. That is a convenient identity, not a model, and it will misprice a team whose scoring rate differs from its margin.|Medium. It matters for the parlay family and for any prop work.|Fit a third rating pair directly on each team's points scored, then check whether it beats the algebraic split out-of-sample.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-1
A10-S08|Correlation|Re-measure the side/total residual correlation out-of-sample|The published value is in-sample and its confidence interval includes zero, so it cannot yet justify a parlay price adjustment.|Medium. It gates the parlay family.|Use walk-forward residuals rather than in-sample residuals and re-publish with n and CI.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-1
A10-S09|Validation|Pre-register every strategy parameter before the season resumes|The walk-forward results in this pack were produced after the fact, on data already in hand. That is a valid backtest but it is not the same as a pre-registered one.|Medium-high as a discipline. It is the difference between a backtest and a forecast.|Write the parameter set to a file with a timestamp and hash it before the next week's numbers are captured.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/scores/2026/week-1
A10-S10|Props|Treat the player-prop family as blocked, not deferred|No official NFL page publishes prop lines. Registering the family without a data route invites someone to fill it in later with non-official numbers.|Medium as a safeguard.|Keep A9-S10 in the leaderboard with a blocked status until a data route exists, and re-open only when nextgenstats or a licensed feed is available.|not_started|https://nextgenstats.nfl.com/
A10-S11|Governance|Name an owner for promotion and demotion|The demotion gate has six armed rules and no one to fire them.|Low effort, high consequence.|Record the owner in COORDINATION.md and make promotion a logged, timestamped event.|not_started|https://www.nfl.com/injuries/
A10-S12|Data|Ask the shared session that owns scripts/source_coverage.py to add the NFL domains|NFL.com rows are currently reported as secondary_reference_only because the publisher list has no NFL entry, which understates the provenance of every row in this pack.|Low effort, affects how this pack is audited.|Log a cross-session request in COORDINATION.md rather than editing the shared file.|requested_via_coordination|https://www.nfl.com/standings/league/2026/REG
